WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.966
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:09.420
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:16.900
Unit one: Present Simple and Present Continuous. Today you will talk about habits, facts and actions happening now.

4
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.003
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.967 --> 00:00:24.292
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.105
Habit.

7
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:29.325
Habit means something you do regularly.

8
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:31.371
Reading is my habit.

9
00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:34.264
Your turn. Say: Habit.

10
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.043
Habit.

11
00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:39.610
Routine.

12
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:43.220
Routine means your usual daily activities.

13
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:45.932
My routine starts at six.

14
00:00:46.517 --> 00:00:48.844
Your turn. Say: Routine.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.620
Routine.

16
00:00:53.383 --> 00:00:54.442
Always.

17
00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.252
Always means every time.

18
00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.687
She always walks to school.

19
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:03.145
Your turn. Say: Always.

20
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.129
Always.

21
00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:08.919
Usually.

22
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:11.870
Usually means most of the time.

23
00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:13.972
We usually eat rice.

24
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:17.027
Your turn. Say: Usually.

25
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:20.786
Usually.

26
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.307
Now.

27
00:01:23.317 --> 00:01:24.852
Now means at this moment.

28
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:26.730
He is studying now.

29
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:29.679
Your turn. Say: Now.

30
00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:33.395
Now.

31
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.209
At the moment.

32
00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:37.845
At the moment means right now.

33
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.113
I am cooking at the moment.

34
00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:43.253
Your turn. Say: At the moment.

35
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.101
At the moment.

36
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.607
Fact.

37
00:01:49.617 --> 00:01:51.523
Fact means something that is true.

38
00:01:52.117 --> 00:01:54.639
Water boils at 100 degrees.

39
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.786
Your turn. Say: Fact.

40
00:02:00.633 --> 00:02:01.483
Fact.

41
00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.263
Third person.

42
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.331
Third person means he, she or it.

43
00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:08.730
The third person takes -s.

44
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:11.551
Your turn. Say: Third person.

45
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.540
Third person.

46
00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:20.019
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.883 --> 00:02:23.231
Visal, when do we use the present simple?

48
00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:36.376
We use it for habits, routines and facts. For example, I go to school every day, and the sun rises in the east. With he, she or it we add -s to the verb.

49
00:02:37.483 --> 00:02:39.193
And the present continuous?

50
00:02:40.283 --> 00:02:53.057
We use am, is or are plus the -ing form for actions happening now, such as I am writing, or for temporary situations such as She is staying with her aunt this week.

51
00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.848
Which words help me choose?

52
00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:06.455
Words like always, usually and every day go with the present simple. Words like now, at the moment and look! go with the present continuous.

53
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.263
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.117 --> 00:03:17.364
Grammar focus: Present simple: V and Vs; present continuous: am and is and are plus V-ing.

55
00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:18.874
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.583 --> 00:03:21.571
She goes to school every day.

57
00:03:22.483 --> 00:03:24.460
She is studying in the library now.

58
00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:32.653
Habits and facts use the present simple. Actions now use am, is or are plus verb-ing. Look at the time words to choose.

59
00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:37.323
Be careful! Don't say: She go to school every day.

60
00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.661
Say: She goes to school every day.

61
00:03:41.961 --> 00:03:43.670
Add -s with he, she, it.

62
00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:47.270
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.300
Sokha's Morning.

64
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.981
Sokha usually gets up at six o'clock every day.

65
00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.175
He eats rice and fish for breakfast.

66
00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:59.793
At the moment he is walking to school with his friend.

67
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.800
His friend is carrying a big bag.

68
00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.811
They always arrive before the bell.

69
00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:10.983
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:13.863
She blank to school every day.

71
00:04:14.163 --> 00:04:17.746
A, go. B, goes. C, is going.

72
00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.033
The answer is B: goes.

73
00:04:24.183 --> 00:04:26.685
Look! The children blank in the yard.

74
00:04:26.985 --> 00:04:30.487
A, are playing. B, plays. C, play.

75
00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:35.986
The answer is A: are playing.

76
00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.405
Water blank at 100 degrees.

77
00:04:39.705 --> 00:04:43.103
A, boils. B, is boiling. C, boil.

78
00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:48.701
The answer is A: boils.

79
00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:52.569
Which word goes with the present continuous?

80
00:04:52.869 --> 00:04:56.360
A, every day. B, now. C, always.

81
00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.551
The answer is B: now.

82
00:05:02.717 --> 00:05:04.751
What is Sokha doing at the moment?

83
00:05:05.051 --> 00:05:09.099
A, eating rice. B, sleeping. C, walking to school.

84
00:05:12.633 --> 00:05:14.923
The answer is C: walking to school.

85
00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:19.343
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.183 --> 00:05:24.157
Tell me about your daily routine and what you are doing now.

87
00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.381
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:34.681 --> 00:05:44.859
I usually get up at six o'clock and eat breakfast with my family. Then I go to school by bicycle. At the moment I am answering a question in English class.

89
00:05:45.159 --> 00:05:46.996
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:47.883 --> 00:05:56.701
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present simple: v and vs; present continuous: am and is and are plus v-ing.

91
00:05:57.001 --> 00:06:02.207
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

92
00:06:02.507 --> 00:06:05.020
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

93
00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.856
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

